# Frontend build

When you change anything under `frontend/` (source, `public/`, Vite config, etc.), **before finishing the task** run a production build:

```bash
cd frontend
npm run build
```

If the build fails, fix the errors and re-run until it passes.

## After a successful build

`postbuild` runs `scripts/git-sync-after-build.mjs` (cleans `dist/assets` churn, stages `frontend/src` + `public` + `dist/css`).

Agents: always run `npm run build` — do not copy files into `dist` by hand.

Only commit `frontend/dist/assets` + `index.html` when the user explicitly asks to ship a full frontend deploy bundle.
